                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-133",
                                    "linecount": 2,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 90.0, 860.0, 290.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "The Volume~ and Mix~ subpatchers allow for (overdriven) gain and dry/wet adjustments."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-38",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 90.0, 590.0, 70.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Description"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-19",
                                    "linecount": 5,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 90.0, 780.0, 290.0, 78.0 ],
                                    "text": "In parallel, the envelope is mapped to an adjustable frequency range in the MapToFilterFrequency~ subpatcher, to control the center frequency of a state-variable filter (SVFilter~ subpatcher), applied to the output sound."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-15",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 90.0, 730.0, 290.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "The amplitude is sent to the Envelope~ subpatcher, which smoothens the volume envelope in order to scale the output of the oscillators."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-6",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 90.0, 680.0, 290.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "The frequency is sent to the Oscillators~ subpatcher, which contains a set of oscillators whose timbre, detuning and stereo image can be adjusted."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-4",
                                    "linecount": 4,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 90.0, 610.0, 290.0, 64.0 ],
                                    "text": "The Analysis~ subpatcher performs pitch and amplitude estimations, and outputs a frequency (in Hz) and a linear amplitude - which are forwarded to rnbo~'s rightmost outlet for display purposes."
                                }
                            },
