                                    "patching_rect": [ 536.0, 178.0, 24.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "ms"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 330.0, 135.0, 20.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "ct"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-23",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 220.0, 135.0, 20.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "st"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-17",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 536.0, 267.0, 70.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "50 ms ramp"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-10",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 572.0, 231.0, 51.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "samples"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-157",
                                    "linecount": 2,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 580.0, 370.0, 35.0 ],
                                    "text": "Also check the Switch~ subpatcher, which embeds a small mechanism that avoids sound artefacts when no transposition is set."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-107",
                                    "linecount": 5,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 500.0, 344.0, 78.0 ],
                                    "text": "As we're using two pitch shifters - one for each audio channel - it's easy to slightly alter each channel independantly, in order to produce stereo detuning effects (Spread parameter). The rate~ object time-scales the output of phasor~ in order to detune the Right channel symmetrically."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-106",
                                    "linecount": 4,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 430.0, 300.0, 64.0 ],
                                    "text": "Finally we need to calculate the frequency of phasor~ according to some musical arguments. In the FreqCalc subpatcher, we're converting semi-tones and cents to frequency, relatively to the actual Window size."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-105",
                                    "linecount": 7,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 320.0, 333.0, 107.0 ],
                                    "text": "The output of phasor~ is used in two ways. First it is adjusted to run between the bounds of the Window range to control the delay time. The output of phasor~ also reads synchronously in a \"Welch\" wavetable, whose output is used as an amplitude envelope for the delay line - the envelope is zero at the points where the sawtooth wraps around, and in between, rises smoothly to a maximum value of 1."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-104",
                                    "linecount": 8,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 190.0, 332.0, 122.0 ],
                                    "text": "However, we can't maintain the transposition forever. We need to create a copy of our delay line, and a mechanism that allows envelope \"windowing\" between the two delay lines, the second one running halfway out of phase. We then need to define fixed intervals of time broken by discontinuous changes. This amount of time is defined by the Window parameter, and multiplies the continuous [0. 1] output range of a sawtooth generator (the phasor~ object)."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-103",
                                    "linecount": 6,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 90.0, 321.0, 93.0 ],
                                    "text": "To alter the pitch of an incoming sound, it is possible to use variable delay lines (the delay~ object) that reproduce the Doppler effect. To maintain a fixed musical interval of transposition over a length of time, it is necessary to alter the pitch in a continuous fashion. That's the role of the phasor~ object embedded in the present patcher."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-86",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 595.0, 183.0, 78.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "Translate milliseconds to samples"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-16",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 700.0, 70.0, 70.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Description"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-68",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 170.0, 31.0, 144.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "Adjusts the pitch shifting (in semi-tones) applied to the input signals"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-65",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 385.0, 200.0, 32.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Rate"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-71",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 310.0, 31.0, 140.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "Adjusts a pitch detuning (in cents) between the left and right channels"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-72",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 362.0, 115.0, 45.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Spread"
                                }
                            },
